From: RG405M port <rg405m@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: sprd: use the slave port window size as the transfer step

The vendor (Unisoc 5.4) sprd-dma driver takes the source/destination step from
src_port_window_size/dst_port_window_size when set, and only falls back to the bus
width otherwise. Mainline always uses the bus width.

The sprd VBC PCM driver plays interleaved stereo with one DMA channel per channel
(2-byte samples, 4-byte frames) and asks for a 4-byte source step. With the bus width
(2 bytes) each channel read L and R alternately into its FIFO, so on the RG405M every
sound played exactly one octave low, with a discontinuity at each period (measured:
1 kHz -> 500 Hz, 20 ms breaks; stock Android plays 1000.0 Hz from the same file).

Users that do not set a port window size are unchanged.

--- a/drivers/dma/sprd-dma.c	2026-09-30 22:46:31.071949584 +0900
+++ b/drivers/dma/sprd-dma.c	2026-09-30 22:46:31.118749581 +0900
@@ -772,7 +772,17 @@
 	phys_addr_t llist_ptr;
 
 	if (dir == DMA_MEM_TO_DEV) {
-		src_step = sprd_dma_get_step(slave_cfg->src_addr_width);
+		/*
+		 * A non-zero port window is the source stride. The Unisoc VBC
+		 * playback path runs one DMA channel per channel over interleaved
+		 * PCM (16-bit samples, 4-byte frames): each channel must step 4
+		 * bytes. Stepping by the sample width fed L and R alternately into
+		 * one FIFO -- audio one octave low with a glitch every period.
+		 * Same as the vendor 5.4 driver.
+		 */
+		src_step = slave_cfg->src_port_window_size ?
+			   slave_cfg->src_port_window_size :
+			   sprd_dma_get_step(slave_cfg->src_addr_width);
 		if (src_step < 0) {
 			dev_err(sdev->dma_dev.dev, "invalid source step\n");
 			return src_step;
@@ -788,7 +798,9 @@
 		else
 			dst_step = SPRD_DMA_NONE_STEP;
 	} else {
-		dst_step = sprd_dma_get_step(slave_cfg->dst_addr_width);
+		dst_step = slave_cfg->dst_port_window_size ?
+			   slave_cfg->dst_port_window_size :
+			   sprd_dma_get_step(slave_cfg->dst_addr_width);
 		if (dst_step < 0) {
 			dev_err(sdev->dma_dev.dev, "invalid destination step\n");
 			return dst_step;
